# ChangeLog

## Unreleased (2026-07-23)

### Bug Fixes
- Windows: file paths with non-ASCII characters now work for loading, screenshots, SD images and recording
- Mid-frame NR $15 layer-priority changes now render per scanline instead of at frame-end value
- Sprite tie: NR $34 no longer clobbers the pattern bit; port-to-mirror reverse sync implemented

### Internal JNEXT Development
- Harness self-tests extended: real cleanup bodies, packaging failure-path reporting, bounded selftest invocations

## v0.99.0 (2026-07-23)

### User Features
- LoRes 128x96 video layer: 8-bit and Radastan 4-bit modes now render
- macOS: a self-contained `jnext.app` that runs without Homebrew installed
- MP4 recording now works in the Windows build
- `--sdcard-readonly` opens the SD card read-only, so a run cannot alter a shared image

### Bug Fixes
- `--record` now exits non-zero when FFmpeg fails or produces an empty MP4
- Ports `$FF3B` (ULA+ Data) and `$243B` now return the driven value, not a fixed zero
- ULA palette entries above the standard range no longer show invented colours
- NEX files with LoRes, Hi-Res or Hi-Colour screens load both halves correctly
- Sprite pattern index re-bases correctly for tied (composite) sprites
- CTC control-word interrupt-enable bit now reaches the interrupt fabric
- Tape EAR idle level corrected; the Z80N `NEXTREG` register latch fixed
- macOS bundle now includes the SDL3 library it loads at runtime

### Internal JNEXT Development
- LoRes compliance test plan: 91 VHDL-cited rows, written before the implementation
- Every test run gets a private SD-card image copy, so runs cannot disturb each other
- `roms/` holds only the boot ROM; jnext provisions the SD image itself
- Packaging suite runs green in CI and is now a release gate

## v0.98.72 (2026-07-20)

### Bug Fixes
- User guide is now actually installed by every package, under the docs directory
- Guide links now work when opened from disk; they previously needed a web server

## v0.98.71 (2026-07-20)

### User Features
- New nine-chapter user guide, shipped with every package and readable offline
- New jnext(1) man page in every package; USAGE.md generated from the same source
- Preferences "Apply" no longer restarts the emulated machine

### Developer Features
- Debugger window attaches to the emulator window and follows it as you move it
- Attachment works on X11; unavailable on Wayland, which cannot position windows

### Bug Fixes
- Rewind recorded nothing after a program wrote port 0xFF or received a UART byte
- Soundrive DAC buzz was a bug in the bundled demo, not the emulator

### Internal JNEXT Development
- CI runs in a Fedora 44 container using the same make targets as a local run
- Fixed piped make commands hiding test failures; CI had reported a failing run green
- CLI flag set is now a data table, checked against the man page both ways
- docs-check gates man page, USAGE.md and the rendered guide on every test run
- Traceability matrix VHDL citations script-generated: 1608 uncited rows down to 579
- Unit suites: 5340 rows across 65 suites, zero skips

## v0.98.56 (2026-07-19)

### User Features
- Mouse now usable: click the screen to capture the pointer, Ctrl+Alt to release
- Mega Drive 6-button pads: the X / Y / Z / MODE buttons are now readable by programs
- The 16 extended keys (cursors, EDIT, DELETE, BREAK, EXTEND MODE, ...) are readable in raw form
- New key bindings: Esc = BREAK, Tab = EXTEND MODE, Alt+E / G / C = EDIT / GRAPH / CAPS LOCK
- Each joystick port can be driven by a gamepad or by the cursor keys + Space
- USB gamepads now work in the Qt GUI, not just the SDL-only build
- Frames paced to the exact machine period; never-displayed frames are no longer drawn
- `--esxdos-stub`: `run NAME.nex` chain-loads a sibling NEX, plus in-memory esxDOS file I/O

### Developer Features
- esxDOS / NextZXOS syscall tracing
- `--wav-record FILE`: record stereo audio to WAV, no audio device or ffmpeg needed
- `--dac-trace FILE`: timestamped DAC channel writes to CSV
- Per-second frame tick diagnostics (interval, emulation, queue, paint) for stutter analysis
- `tools/extract-sdcard-nex.sh`: extract every NEX on an SD image into a testable tree

### Bug Fixes
- Mouse reached only a small part of the screen, and varied with where the pointer entered
- Mouse buttons could stay stuck down if capture was released mid-drag
- Extended-key and MD extra-button registers returned nothing to any program
- Tilemap raster splits now land on the exact scanline
- SD image patching at first start no longer looks frozen

### Internal JNEXT Development
- Regression harness split into a shared library plus one script per test
- CI builds all four Qt-UI x debugger combinations; two were silently broken
- Library dependencies declared properly; the build no longer relies on debugger link order
- Test runs always rebuild the emulator binary, so no suite can report on a stale build
- Pull-request review and merge protocol documented

## v0.98.34 (2026-07-17)

### User Features
- macOS support: jnext now builds and runs natively on macOS (the macOS build previously failed to compile)

### Internal JNEXT Development
- macOS build fixes: debug library links SDL2 for Homebrew's header layout; boot ROM embedded as a portable C array (no objcopy) so it builds on Linux, Windows and macOS alike
- New manual "macOS Build" CI workflow to test the macOS build without cutting a release
- `make publish-release`: pushes commits plus only the newest tag so a GitHub Release reliably triggers

## v0.98.29 (2026-07-17)

### Bug Fixes
- Reset (Reset button / F1 / a program's own reset) now re-boots to NextZXOS instead of crashing to 48K BASIC; loading a program from the menu resets the machine to a clean state first
- Flatpak GUI now launches (its runtime's compiler miscompiled the Qt startup under LTO)

### Internal JNEXT Development
- Reset modelled as a host power-on cold boot (reconstruct + re-run the startup path); debugger breakpoints survive a reset
- Flatpak: LTO disabled as a documented toolchain workaround and moved to the org.kde 6.10 runtime; CI bundle is versioned
- Release protocol: AppStream metainfo lists only public releases; every bump prompts whether to publish; a public release requires a differential ChangeLog entry

## v0.98.24 (2026-07-16)

### User Features
- Install packages for every supported platform: Fedora/RHEL (RPM), Debian/Ubuntu 24.04 & 26.04 (DEB), Flatpak, and a self-contained Windows (x64) zip
- Windows build is portable (all Qt/SDL runtime bundled) and no longer opens a stray console window
- Preferences dialog (Settings → Preferences) with settings saved to `~/.jnext`
- New application icon

### Developer Features
- `make package-{rpm,deb,flatpak,win,src}` build every distributable locally; documented in BUILD.md

### Bug Fixes
- RPM now installs on Fedora (was linked against the wrong libcurl); DEB now installs on Ubuntu 26 (built per-LTS for 24.04 and 26.04)
- Frame pacing follows the emulated 50/60 Hz video refresh (issue #9)
- Oversized/extended NEX files are rejected with a clear message instead of misbehaving (issue #10)
- Windows: SD-image download no longer fails certificate verification; fixed a startup stack overflow

### Internal JNEXT Development
- Gated release protocol: `releases.yaml` allowlist, one consolidated CI release workflow, and RELEASE-PROTOCOL.md
- `version.yaml` is the single source of truth; every bump propagates the version into all packaging files
- Each package builds on its native distro; Flatpak and Windows build inside Fedora containers in CI, Flatpak from the local checkout
- Task 69 integration test plan + CI with honest SD-image provisioning + README status badges; config relocated to `~/.jnext`

## v0.98.3 (2026-07-15)

### User Features
- Emulation ~2.8× faster end-to-end: 400% turbo now runs ~284 FPS in Next mode (was ~100), well past 200
- 48K-class machines (BIFROST/NIRVANA-style engines) run over 2.7× as fast
- Rewind is now opt-in (`--rewind-buffer-size N`): default runs use ~1 GB less RAM and start faster
- Rewind can be switched on live from the debugger — no restart needed
- At turbo speeds the GUI skips composing frames nobody sees, smoothing high-speed runs
- Joystick, mouse and keyboard state now survive a rewind correctly

### Developer Features
- `--benchmark N`: headless throughput measurement (T-states/sec), plus a `make bench` harness with locked, spread-checked medians
- `--trace` enables the instruction trace log independently of rewind
- Debugger refuses to resume/step a machine left corrupt by a failed rewind, warning first at every resume path

### Bug Fixes
- GUI no longer crashes at startup on X11 desktops with a session manager (Ubuntu/LMDE, issue #8)
- Debugger single-stepping now delivers CTC/UART/frame interrupts exactly like free-running execution
- Corrupted rewind snapshots are detected (per-subsystem sentinels) and refuse to load a torn machine, pausing loudly instead
- Sprite collision/overtime bits (port 0x303B) stay correct at turbo speeds
- IM2 peripheral interrupt-pulse timing was 8× too fast below 28 MHz — now speed-invariant per the VHDL

### Internal JNEXT Development
- Profile-guided optimization campaign across two waves, 23 independently reviewed merges: LTO on release (the single biggest win), copper/compositor/tilemap hot-spot rewrites, per-instruction device-tick fixes
- Final optimization report (`doc/design/TASK27-FINAL-OPTIMIZATION-REPORT.md`) with measured per-stage gains
- Bare `cmake` builds can no longer silently produce an unoptimized (-O0) binary
- State snapshots gained bounds checks; the dead Saveable interface removed
- Test dashboard is now a deterministic artifact regenerated from the suite manifest (no more stale counts / merge conflicts)

## v0.98.0 (2026-07-14)

### User Features
- Tape saving: BASIC `SAVE` writes a real `.tap` file (`--tape-save FILE`)
- DeciLoad 12k8 turbo-loaded games now load, both from TZX Direct-Recording blocks and from WAV
- `--silent` disables all sound output (about 10% faster emulation)

### Developer Features
- `--delayed-automatic-exit-frames`: frame-exact automatic exit for scripted runs
- `--delayed-keypress-frames` extended: named keys, punctuation, shift combos, repeatable; unknown keys fail loudly

### Bug Fixes
- Multicolour engines (BIFROST, NIRVANA) render correctly: contention pattern had the wrong period, attribute fetches were early
- Contention window was displaced 64 scanlines on 48K/128K/+3 — timing now matches real-hardware measurements
- Real-time TZX/WAV tape playback had been silently frozen for some time: the tape clock reset every frame
- Runtime video-timing changes (NR 0x03 machine timing, NR 0x05 50/60 Hz) now commit at the frame edge, readback included
- Mid-frame ULA clip window and Layer 2 transparency changes now apply on the correct scanline
- Soundrive Mode-2 sample ports no longer swallow 128K paging writes when disabled, and suppress them when enabled, as hardware does
- Debugger audio mute checkboxes now actually mute their source

### Internal JNEXT Development
- 17 new screenshot regressions: BIFROST/NIRVANA FUSE-verified on 48K/128K/+3, DeciLoad TZX+WAV, NextZXOS dot-command, tape-save boot guard
- Unit-suite skips down to 10 (all snapshot-schema); every Memory/MMU, NMI and port-dispatch skip closed
- Real FUSE driven headless and scripted as a T-state oracle — located both contention root causes

## v0.97.0 (2026-07-13)

### User Features
- Run a program by name: `jnext game.tap` now works exactly like `--load game.tap`

### Developer Features
- Debugger video panel gains "All layers" (the composed picture) and "Background colour" views
- `--delayed-screenshot-layers` captures any subset of ULA / Layer 2 / sprites / tilemap
- The two ULA views now say which screen bank the ULA is actually reading
- Per-subsystem log levels, e.g. `--log-level cpu=trace,video=warn`

### Bug Fixes
- Stepping through a frame no longer corrupts the emulation: the Copper and every raster split were being wiped
- Debugger no longer reports Layer 2 disabled when a program enables it through port 0x123B
- Debugger's NextREG panel no longer disturbs the Pi-I2S sample the program is about to read
- Debugger video panels fixed: wrong memory bank, no per-scanline replay, and one panel corrupted live scroll state
- A screenshot that cannot be written is now an error with a non-zero exit, not a silent success

### Internal JNEXT Development
- Test suites are declared in config files with pinned row counts: a missing test is a loud failure, never a silent skip
- Two unit-test suites that had never once run now run — 63 assertions no count had ever included
- The test harness is itself under test: 26 self-test cases, run by every regression
- ccache wired into the build: a clean rebuild drops from 65 s to 9 s
- Test results no longer depend on the user's locale

## v0.96.0 (2026-07-12)

### Bug Fixes
- Constant noise/buzz throughout a session fixed — the audio device was starved and SDL filled the gaps with silence (issue #7)
- Clicking over beeper music fixed; worst on machines with little CPU headroom, which is why issue #7 was reported as a constant hum
- Beeper music no longer has a high-pitched tone over it: the mixer is sampled by integration instead of point-sampling (aliasing)
- Emulation now paces on the sound card's clock, so audio never drifts ahead of or behind the emulator

### Internal JNEXT Development
- Reverted the v0.95.x DC-blocking mixer stage: it never fixed issue #7, it masked it, and it distorted beeper waveforms
- New audio-underrun regression test captures jnext's real audio output and fails if silence is ever spliced into the stream

## v0.95.0 (2026-07-11)

### User Features
- SD card is now optional: with no --sdcard, jnext finds, or offers to download and patch, the official NextZXOS image
- Download progress dialog while the distribution image is fetched
- SD-card flag renamed to --sdcard (the old --sd-card is still accepted)

### Developer Features
- --rtc pins the emulated real-time clock to a fixed date/time for deterministic boot screenshots
- --sdcard-download-confirm / --sdcard-download-force control the built-in image download

### Bug Fixes
- NextZXOS mid-boot colour-garbage glitch fixed (bank 5 is now dedicated VRAM, un-aliased from external SRAM)
- SD/SPI card responses conform to spec (2 idle bytes before R1, no $FF in CMD58 reply, real CRC-16 data checksums)
- Multiface memory window backed by external SRAM on the Next, matching hardware
- +3 machine-type register reports the VHDL cold-boot default

### Internal JNEXT Development
- Firmware-bypass route (--bypass-tbblue-fw) and its tooling removed now that native boot works
- Host-side SD-image formatting rebuilt on vendored ChaN FatFs; downloads via libcurl; SHA256 integrity guard on the cached image
- Boot-to-menu screenshot regressions added; unit tests 4232 pass / 0 fail, regression 46/0/0

## v0.94.0 (2026-07-10)

### User Features
- NextZXOS boots natively from the SD card image through the authentic FPGA boot chain (welcome screen + main menu)
- Instant TAP loading via phantom typist, plus FUSE-style fastload mode
- Pristine z88dk NEX games boot without patching via the esxDOS stub option
- Host hotkeys for hardware buttons: Multiface NMI, DivMMC NMI, soft and hard reset
- Per-scanline render-state replay (palette, sprites, tilemap, ULA) enables demo-class raster effects
- Mouse: host cursor hidden over the emulator window, position scaling fixed

### Developer Features
- CPU T-state profiler with per-physical-address counters and z88dk map-file heatmap script
- Headless automation: delayed keypress injection and compositor per-pixel trace dump
- Env-gated NextZXOS boot diagnostics (instruction trace ring, trap detector, boot probes)

### Bug Fixes
- Layer 2 320x256 mode no longer shows animated noise on the right half of the screen
- Inverted ULA attributes in Next mode fixed
- Kempston mouse Y axis now uses Cartesian convention
- Bank-7 memory no longer aliases the alt-ROM area (fixed NextZXOS workspace corruption)
- Standalone 128K/+3 machines keep bank 7 intact after Next machine switches
- SD card: open multi-block reads survive chip-select release; single card no longer answers both slots
- Builds cleanly on Debian 12 / GCC 12 from a fresh clone

### Internal JNEXT Development
- Full-subsystem VHDL-conformance audit waves with enumeration-table mandate; hundreds of fixes landed
- Unit-test SKIP-reduction: dashboard grew to 4116 cases at 99% pass, zero failures
- Screenshot regression suite expanded from 30 to 43 cases
- Symmetric-trace differential debugging against reference emulators (CSpect plugin, zx_go harness)
- Multiface core subsystem modelled and VHDL-verified
- Machine ID now reports real-hardware value; soft reset preserves the Z80 register file per VHDL

## v0.93.0

### Bug Fixes
- CTC channel chaining now uses ring topology (ch3→ch0) matching VHDL
- +3 ROM-high bit via port 0x1FFD now observable + NR 0x82 bit 3 gating
- Specdrum port 0xDF read handler for VHDL port_1f combo gate
- I2C ACK phase off-by-one — read data was shifted left by one bit

### Internal JNEXT Development
- Unit tests: 2556 pass, 0 fail, 696 skip (3252 total across 19 suites)
- Regression suite: 34/34 clean
- Uniform test output format across all 19 test suites
- Color-coded `make unit-test` target with per-suite totals
- Version bumping procedure documented in CLAUDE.md

## v0.92.0

### User Features
- 640px native framebuffer for tilemap 80-col and Layer 2 640x256 modes
- Floating bus emulation enabled for all machine types
- Compositor blend modes 110 (additive) and 111 (subtractive)
- Pentagon, Kempston joystick, mouse, and ULA+ ports now respond

### Developer Features
- Debugger: improved interrupt and tilemap split-screen debugging

### Bug Fixes
- Z80 instruction timing and contention fixes — games now run at correct speed
- NEX loader: palette, sprite, transparency, and init fixes
- Tilemap rendering, scrolling, control-bit swap, and 80-col pixel addressing
- Compositor NR 0x14 palette-compare transparency for ULA and Layer 2
- Port dispatch exclusive routing and VHDL-correct decode masks
- NR 0x82-0x85 port-enable register defaults and gating
- DivMMC mapram OR-latch, read_control mask, ROM3 automap gating
- DMA prescaler, ULA frame timing, AY envelope, SPI decode, MMU reset

### Internal JNEXT Development
- Subsystem compliance tests: 1150/1171 pass (98%)
- Regression suite: 34/34 clean
- 15 emulator fixes + 9 test reclassifications across 21 backlog items

## v0.91.0

### User Features
- ZX Spectrum 48K, 128K, +2A/+3, Pentagon, and Next machine types
- ULA, Layer 2 (256/320/640), Sprites (8-bit/4-bit), Tilemap, Copper
- 6-mode layer compositor with per-scanline border colour
- 8 palettes with 9-bit RGB (512 colours)
- AY/YM x3 TurboSound, 4-channel DAC, Beeper
- NEX, SNA, SZX, TAP, TZX, WAV, RZX file formats
- Qt 6 GUI: Hi-DPI, fullscreen, CRT filter, speed control, screenshots, MPEG4 video recording

### Developer Features
- Debugger: registers, disassembly, hex editor, breakpoints, trace, symbol tables
- Magic breakpoint (ED FF / DD 01) and magic debug port
- Headless mode for automated testing and screenshot regression suite
- Backwards execution: Step Back, Frame Back, rewind slider

### Bug Fixes
- (initial release)

### Internal JNEXT Development
- FUSE-based Z80 core with Z80N extensions (26 opcodes)
- Memory contention for 48K, 128K, +3, Pentagon timing models
- IM1/IM2 interrupt controller with 14 Next interrupt levels
- DivMMC with automap, CTC, UART, DMA, SPI, I2C/RTC peripherals
